+"keep going", "keep investigating", or "continue" an investigation they already
+requested, and do NOT report that you are out of tool calls or rounds — you have no
+quota to announce, and such a question hands the work back without delivering any
+of it.
+
+If a request named specific identifiers (a file path, catalog item, GUID, account,
+host), those identifiers ARE the specification: the request is not ambiguous, so go
+fetch them rather than asking. Before ending a turn with any requested fact still
+missing, check whether an explicitly named route is still untried — if one is, make
+that call instead of asking a question. If you genuinely cannot obtain a fact, state
+plainly which fact is missing and what you tried; that is an answer. "Shall I
+continue?" is not.
